20. DEVELOPMENT STRATEGY

Build the complete game through sequential, verifiable milestones.

Milestone 1: Project foundation, preload flow, main menu, responsive rendering, shared HUD, and settings.

Milestone 2: Explorer animations, camera movement, collisions, and Level 1.

Milestone 3: Puzzle chamber and deterministic puzzle mechanics.

Milestone 4: Vehicle chase.

Milestone 5: Time-travel cinematic.

Milestone 6: Shooting mechanics and Level 4.

Milestone 7: Grand Reveal, artifact interaction, and ending.

Milestone 8: Save system, audio integration, testing, performance, and final polish.

After each milestone:

1. Run the application.
2. Check for errors.
3. Test the implemented mechanics.
4. Fix critical issues.
5. Report the actual state of the implementation.
6. Preserve the working code before proceeding.

If the environment has a task or execution limit, prioritize a complete playable vertical slice over an unfinished collection of disconnected scenes. Continue through the milestones whenever possible.

Do not claim all levels are complete if only the main menu or a single level works.

